president's national security adviser  jake sullivan joins us from the white  house to tell us more about this strike  good morning jake i hope all is well  let's jump right into it we just heard  that al-swahiri was downtown kabul with  taliban assistance what does this say  about the relationship between the  taliban and al qaeda  well first we do believe that senior  members of the haqqani network which is  associated with the taliban knew that  zawahiri was in kabul there may have  been other members who didn't and we are  communicating directly with the taliban  about their obligations not to allow al  qaeda  to use afghanistan as a basis for  plotting but let me say this  what it also says is that president  biden's pledged to the american people  that even after pulling american men and  women out of active combat in  afghanistan we would able be able to  take out terrorists in afghanistan he  made good on that pledge this weekend he  showed that we can actually keep america  safe take terrorists off the battlefield  and not have thousands of american men  and women fighting and dying in  afghanistan for 20 years of war that is  a significant success for the  president's strategy and americans can  feel safer today now that the leader of  al-qaeda ayman al-zawahiri is off the  battlefield  jake it's vlad uh so you just confirmed  that the taliban was aware that azuahiri  was in kabul so if the taliban continues  to harbor terrorists what is the united  states prepared to do what is president  biden prepared to do well we are  communicating as i said directly with  the taliban about their obligations to  live up to their commitments and also  our capacity to hold them accountable  for not living up to their commitments  because we're not obviously just going  to take their word for it we proved that  this weekend by taking out al-zawahiri  and we're prepared to take further  action to ensure that afghanistan can  never again be used as a basis for  attacking americans that may have  sounded like just words a year ago but  today  it's words backed up by swift and  decisive action if there is someone  plotting in afghanistan against the  united states or if there is an al-qaida  leader trying to inspire attacks against  america and americans as zawahiri was  doing we will find them and we will take  them out and we just did that and the  president has shown the wisdom strength  and success of his policy  in this action that he ordered over the  weekend  national security adviser jake sullivan  thank you
 

